Wavelength Fabric

Copyright 2026 Summon Software Labs

Wavelength Fabric is an open-source, vendor-neutral runtime for wavelength and
channel allocation, reservation, authority, conflict detection, and lifecycle
over abstract optical spectrum resources.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Wavelength Fabric does not control optical hardware. It does not own physical
connectivity lifecycle, transceiver identity, route computation across optical
resources, or measured link quality. Those concerns belong to adjacent
runtimes, and Wavelength Fabric consumes their facts only through narrow,
explicitly supplied inputs.

Wavelength Fabric does not collect or transmit any telemetry. All telemetry is
written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the machine
running the software.

Wavelength Fabric accepts contributions from individuals and organizations on
the terms of the Apache License 2.0 without requiring a Contributor License
Agreement (CLA). See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution guidance.
